---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy | MuscleQuest" path="/privacy-policy/"
  description="How MuscleQuest collects, uses and protects your data, and the choices you have."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Privacy policy", path: "/privacy-policy/" }])]}>
  <Prose>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: 1 November 2026</strong></p>
    <p>
      Thank you for using <strong>MuscleQuest</strong>. We value your privacy and are committed to protecting your
      personal data. This privacy policy outlines how we collect, use, and safeguard your information when you use
      our app.
    </p>

    <h2 id="information">1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect the following types of information to provide and improve our services:</p>

    <h3>a. Personal Information</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account Information</strong>: Account creation in <strong>MuscleQuest</strong> is optional. If you
        choose to create an account using Google OAuth, we collect your name, email address and profile photo from
        your Google account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Workout Data</strong>: Your workout data is stored locally on your device and will only leave your
        device if you choose to create a backup or share it with friends.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Social Features</strong>: Friends and sharing are optional and require an account. Your display
        name and profile photo are visible to your friends, to people who search for your exact email address, and
        to anyone you send a friend request to or receive one from. Your email address is stored with your account
        and other users never see it. A one-way hash of it lets people who already know your exact address find
        you. Plans, workouts, custom exercises, workout history, body measurements and strength progress are
        shared only if you turn on sharing for that category in the app, or for a single plan or workout, and only
        with your friends.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>b. Device and Diagnostic Information</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Device Information</strong>: General data related to your device model, operating system version,
        language and app version, and diagnostic information.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="use">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use the collected information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the app.</li>
      <li>Personalise the user experience.</li>
      <li>Communicate with you regarding updates and app-related notifications.</li>
      <li>Analyse app stability and performance for optimisation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="sharing">3. How We Share Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>MuscleQuest</strong> does not sell or share your personal data with third parties, except in the
      following cases:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service Providers</strong>: We may share limited data with trusted service providers that assist
        us in operating the app: Supabase Inc. for accounts, backup storage and social features (hosted in
        Ireland, EU), Google for sign-in, Cloudflare for delivering exercise animations and app configuration,
        Bugsnag (SmartBear) for error reports and performance data, and Expo for app updates, crash reports and
        performance data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your Friends</strong>: If you use the social features, your display name and profile photo are
        visible to your friends, to people who search for your exact email address, and to anyone you send a
        friend request to or receive one from. Plans, workouts, custom exercises, workout history, body
        measurements and strength progress are shared with your friends only for the categories, or the single
        plans and workouts, where you turn sharing on in the app.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal Requirements</strong>: We may disclose your information if required by law or in response to
        valid legal processes.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="security">4. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      We take data security seriously and use various technical and administrative measures to protect your
      information. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. We
      strive to use commercially acceptable means to safeguard your data but cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">5. Data Storage and Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Workout Data</strong>: Stored locally on your device. If you opt for a backup, it is stored in
        Supabase Storage in the EU, readable only by your account. Data from the backup is used exclusively for
        restoration.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shared Data</strong>: Data you share with friends is kept until you remove it in the app or delete
        your account. Turning off sharing for a category stops its items being shared automatically but does not
        remove what is already shared; use "Delete all shared data" in the app for that. Copies that friends have
        already added to their own library stay on their devices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Personal Data</strong>: Retained for as long as your account is active or as needed to provide
        services and comply with legal obligations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account Deletion</strong>: <a href="/delete-account/">Deleting your account</a> in the app
        immediately removes your account, profile, friendships, shared data and backups. You choose whether to
        keep the training data on your device. Copies that friends have already added to their own library stay on
        their devices. If you can't use the app, the form on that page takes up to 30 days.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Diagnostics</strong>: Error reports and diagnostics already sent to Bugsnag and Expo are kept for
        those providers' retention periods and are not removed when you delete your account.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rights">6. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access, update, or delete your personal data.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent for data collection where applicable.</li>
      <li>Contact us for any questions or concerns regarding your data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="third-parties">7. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>MuscleQuest</strong> uses third-party services to support core app functionality and diagnostics.
      These services may collect the following categories of data:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Device or other IDs (such as app instance IDs, device identifiers and IP addresses)</li>
      <li>
        Technical data (such as device model, operating system, language, app version, app launch counts, screens
        viewed, and the addresses and timings of network requests)
      </li>
      <li>
        Diagnostics and crash data (such as crash logs, error messages, stack traces and app startup performance)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>This data is collected and used for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Authentication and account security (via Supabase Auth with Google sign-in)</li>
      <li>
        Crash reporting, performance monitoring and diagnostics to identify and fix technical issues (via Bugsnag
        and EAS Observe from Expo)
      </li>
      <li>Delivering exercise animations and app configuration (via Cloudflare)</li>
      <li>
        Delivering app updates and counting app launches by platform and app version (via Expo Application
        Services)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Data collected by these services may be associated with your user account or device to help investigate
      issues and improve the app. MuscleQuest does <strong>not</strong> use this data for targeted advertising and
      does <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data. For more information, please review the privacy policies of
      <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase</a>,
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google</a>,
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</a>,
      <a href="https://expo.dev/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Expo</a> and
      <a href="https://docs.bugsnag.com/platforms/android/playstore-privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bugsnag</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="transfer">8. Data Transfer</h2>
    <p>
      Your account, backups and shared data are stored with Supabase in the EU (Ireland), protected by access rules
      that limit each item to you and, for shared data, your friends. Our other service providers may process data
      on servers outside your region or country, which may have different data protection regulations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Versions of MuscleQuest before 2.0 used Google Firebase for accounts, backups, shared data, usage analytics
      and crash reports, and keep doing so until you update. We copy accounts, backups and shared data from
      Firebase to Supabase without any action from you. Once the move is complete we delete them from Firebase,
      including those of accounts deleted in the meantime.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">9. This Website</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views. It does not use cookies, does not track you
      across sites and does not collect personal data. If you use the account deletion form, the name, email
      address and message you enter are sent to us through Formspree so we can process your request.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be communicated by posting the new policy on
      this page with an updated date. Users are advised to review this page periodically for any changes.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact-us">11. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions about this privacy policy, please contact us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email</strong>: <a href="mailto:support@musclequest.app">support@musclequest.app</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Prose>
</BaseLayout>
